    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for firewalld.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 10.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "firewalld is a firewall service daemon that provides a dynamic customizable firewall with a D-Bus interface.\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* firewalld: package upgrade may cause running firewalld to reports errors (JIRA:Rocky Linux-137602)\n\n* [10.3] Firewalld rebase to latest upstream stable (JIRA:Rocky Linux-174658)\n\n* Firewalld --timeout argument does not work for policies (JIRA:Rocky Linux-95705)\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
